  "fixture": "Public environment/path/UUID/time/version/receipt vectors only. Fresh real JVM negative tests. OPS uses fixed fake Java and local static unit syntax verification; no host manager/service/credential changes. FLOCK uses isolated retained regular files, real libc and util-linux2.41.3 with narrow native fault ports. No host lockfile, UID or service mutation.",
  "oracle": "051/PT221..232: bounded nonsecret canonical input, missing/null/unknown rejection, no parsing diagnostics, exact ASCII receipt after owned resource closure, 0/10/50/70 mapping, unexpected runtime escape/fixed fatal message, native admission negatives,64 independent invocations. 018/PT001..008: fixed receipt byte matrix and JVM exit override; all base directives and4 selected previous-key profiles; actual sh/ShellCheck/systemd-analyze with recorded outputs; release classpath/JDBC runtime/Java25 flags. 003/PT-OPS-FLOCK-001..008: independent flock exit20 while Java holds and Java empty while external holds; fcntl does not conflict; one of32 wins; retained original inode remains locked after path replacement; errno11 alone is contention; fixed open flags0x80000/flock6, close once and IO diagnostic redaction.",
  "limitations": "Java coverage belongs to launcher, not a shell percentage. Parent OS flock/inactive/backup/run binding, root-owned environment validation/publication, actual unit credential provisioning and timeout/TERM behavior, full batch, NK CHR and IT/ST are NOT certified. LinuxFileLock is a low-level capability only; root/type/UID/ACL/stable-namespace admission and parent lifecycle are not supplied by it. CLOEXEC is asserted at the native call boundary, not an actual inherited-FD inspection; aarch64 ABI selection only, execution is amd64.",
